# Dashboard UI Agent Rules (Casino Ops + Financial Analytics)
**Stack:** Next.js App Router + shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS v4  
**Goal:** Build a consistent, enterprise-grade operations dashboard for online casino & financial analytics.  
**Priority:** Consistency > aesthetics > novelty. Avoid “creative” UI changes that break architecture.

---

## 0) Non-negotiables (MUST)
1) **Use design tokens only** (CSS variables) for colors/surfaces/borders.  
   - Do NOT hardcode arbitrary colors (e.g. `text-blue-500`) except semantic states via tokens or pre-approved utilities.
2) **Follow layout rhythm**: spacing scale only `4/8/12/16/24/32/48`.  
3) **Typography scale** must be respected (see Section 2).  
4) **Dashboard page structure** is standardized (see Section 3).  
5) **Components must be reusable primitives**; do NOT duplicate UI patterns page by page.  
6) **No flashy gradients, no neon, no heavy shadows**. Enterprise subtle only.
7) **All data numbers must use `tabular-nums`** and stable alignment.
8) **Dark mode must look premium**, not washed-out.

---

## 1) Design System Tokens (Colors, Surfaces, Borders)
### 1.1 Token usage rule
- Use `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.
- Use semantic tokens for states: `--success`, `--warning`, `--danger` and their foreground variants.
- Prefer neutral palettes with one brand accent.

### 1.2 Approved semantic meanings
- **Success** = profit / uptrend / OK / verified
- **Danger** = loss / downtrend / risk / block
- **Warning** = anomaly / attention / pending

### 1.3 Anti-pattern
- ❌ Randomly mixing multiple accent colors in one view.
- ❌ Using saturated gradients to look “cool”.
- ❌ Using inconsistent border colors across cards.

---

## 2) Typography Standard (Hierarchy)
### 2.1 Type scale (Tailwind)
- **Page title:** `text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight`
- **Section title:** `text-lg font-semibold`
- **Body:** `text-sm`
- **Meta/caption:** `text-xs text-muted-foreground`
- **KPI value:** `text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight tabular-nums`
- **Table numbers:** `text-sm tabular-nums`

### 2.2 Rules
- Always include meaningful titles and captions in dashboards.
- Keep text density high but readable.
- Use `leading-relaxed` only for long descriptions; otherwise default leading.

---

## 3) Page Architecture (Standard Dashboard Layout)
Every dashboard-like page MUST follow:
1) **PageHeader**
   - Left: Title + subtitle (context)
   - Right: Global controls (DateRange, Segment tabs, Refresh, Export)
2) **FilterBar** (optional but recommended)
   - tenant/game/currency/status/search
3) **KPI Row** (3–6 cards)
4) **Analytics Row**
   - Charts / heatmaps / trend panels
5) **Data Row**
   - Table (sticky header) + optional RightDrawer for row details
6) **States**
   - Loading skeletons (layout-preserving)
   - Empty states (actionable)
   - Error states (recoverable)

### 3.1 Grid & spacing
- Use a 12-col grid pattern:
  - `grid grid-cols-12 gap-6`
- Cards typically span 3–4 columns depending on density.
- Sections vertical spacing: `space-y-6` or `space-y-8` only.

---

## 4) Component Standards (shadcn/ui)
### 4.1 Must-use primitives
- `Card`, `Badge`, `Button`, `Tabs`, `DropdownMenu`, `Dialog/Drawer`, `Separator`, `Skeleton`, `Table`, `Tooltip`
- Build project primitives in `components/dashboard/*`:
  - `PageHeader`
  - `FilterBar`
  - `KpiCard`
  - `Section`
  - `DataTableShell`
  - `RightDrawer`
  - `Delta` (up/down/flat)
  - `Metric` (label + value + hint)

### 4.2 KPI Card rules
A KPI card must include:
- Label (meta)
- Value (large, tabular-nums)
- Delta (up/down/flat) with semantic color
- Optional: sparkline slot (future extension)
Avoid:
- Decorative icons without meaning
- Long paragraphs inside KPI cards

### 4.3 Table rules
- Sticky header is mandatory for long tables.
- Row height: consistent (`h-10` / `h-11`).
- Numeric columns right-aligned with tabular numbers.
- Use `Badge` for categorical status.
- Clicking a row opens RightDrawer (details, actions, audit trail).

---

## 5) Data Visualization Rules
- Default: clean, minimal charts. No thick grid, no neon.
- Charts must support dark mode well.
- Always include:
  - Axis labels (if meaningful)
  - Tooltip
  - Empty state (no data)
  - Loading skeleton placeholder with fixed height
- Prefer:
  - Area chart for trend
  - Bar for distribution
  - Heatmap for number exposure / risk matrix (casino-style)
- Do NOT introduce new chart libs without approval.

---

## 6) Interaction & UX Rules (Ops-grade)
- Every page must be **actionable**:
  - Filters, drill-down, export, refresh
- Provide:
  - Keyboard focus states
  - Accessible labels for inputs
  - Tooltips for ambiguous metrics
- Avoid:
  - Complex animations
  - Hidden actions without discovery

---

## 7) Tailwind CSS v4 Conventions
- Use semantic classes via tokens:
  - `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`
- Rounding:
  - Use `rounded-xl` or `rounded-2xl` consistently (prefer `rounded-2xl` for primary cards)
- Shadows:
  - Only subtle: `shadow-sm` (or none). No big drop shadows.
- Borders:
  - Prefer borders over heavy shadows for separation.

---

## 8) Next.js App Router Structure (Do not break)
### 8.1 Recommended folder layout
- `app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx` : dashboard shell (sidebar/header)
- `app/(dashboard)/overview/page.tsx`
- `app/(dashboard)/risk/page.tsx`
- `app/(dashboard)/players/page.tsx`
- `components/dashboard/*` : reusable dashboard primitives
- `components/ui/*` : shadcn generated components
- `lib/format/*` : formatters (currency, percent, compact, date)
- `lib/query/*` : query keys, fetchers (no UI)
- `types/*` : domain types

### 8.2 Separation of concerns
- Page components: composition only (layout + wiring).
- UI primitives: styling + structure.
- Domain logic: never inside UI components; place in `lib/` or `domain/`.

---

## 9) Loading / Empty / Error State Standard
### 9.1 Loading
- Use `Skeleton` that matches final layout size.
- No layout shift.

### 9.2 Empty
- Must include:
  - “No data” message
  - Possible reason (filters/time range)
  - CTA: reset filters / expand range

### 9.3 Error
- Show retry button
- Keep UI frame stable

---

## 10) “No Surprise Changes” Policy
Agent must NOT:
- Rename routes or folders without explicit instruction.
- Replace shadcn components with custom ones unless needed.
- Change global tokens or theming unless asked.
- Introduce new libraries without approval.

If uncertain:
- Keep existing architecture and add new primitives instead of rewriting.

---

## 11) Definition of “Professional” (Quality Bar)
The UI must feel like:
- Trading/finance analytics dashboards (high density, clear hierarchy)
- Casino operations monitoring (risk heatmaps, exposure tables, anomaly lists)
Characteristics:
- Consistent spacing + typography
- Neutral surfaces + subtle borders
- Clean tables and controls
- Strong information hierarchy
- Actionable drill-down flows

---

## 12) How to work (Agent Execution Plan)
When implementing a new page:
1) Use existing primitives first.
2) If missing, add ONE new primitive in `components/dashboard/`.
3) Build page composition using standard layout order (Section 3).
4) Add loading/empty/error states.
5) Verify: dark mode, tabular numbers, alignment, density.

Deliverables per page:
- `page.tsx`
- `loading.tsx` (if relevant)
- Any new primitives (minimal)
- No breaking changes to other pages

---

## 13) Quick “Do / Don’t”
✅ Do:
- `tabular-nums`, right-align numeric columns
- sticky header tables
- filter bars, segments, export/refresh
- consistent `gap-6`, `p-6`, `rounded-2xl`
- semantic badges and deltas

❌ Don’t:
- random bright colors
- inconsistent paddings
- big gradients/shadows
- same font size everywhere
- one-off components duplicated across pages
